# Code Quality Rules

## General Principles
- Write clean, minimal code without comments
- Avoid unnecessary verbosity - use fewer tokens
- Prefer short, optimal implementations
- Remove unused imports, variables, and code
- No documentation comments in code files

## Architecture
- Backend: FastAPI with traditional architecture
- Frontend: Next.js with shadcn/ui components
- Follow traditional MVC/MVP patterns
- Keep separation of concerns clear

## Code Style

### Python (FastAPI)
- No docstrings or comments
- Use type hints minimally (only when necessary)
- Prefer list/dict comprehensions over loops
- Use async/await properly
- Keep functions short and focused
- No unnecessary error handling verbosity

### TypeScript/JavaScript (Next.js)
- No comments or JSDoc
- Use functional components
- Prefer arrow functions
- Use shadcn/ui components from @/components/ui
- Keep components small and focused
- Use TypeScript types minimally (infer when possible)

## File Guidelines

### Test Files
- Keep tests minimal and focused
- Only test critical paths
- No verbose test descriptions
- Use concise test names

### Documentation Files
- Minimize markdown files
- Only essential README.md
- No extensive documentation
- Keep it brief and to the point

## What to Avoid
- Comments in code
- Unnecessary documentation
- Verbose variable names
- Redundant code
- Over-engineering
- Unused imports or dependencies
- Excessive type annotations
- Long function names
- Unnecessary abstractions

## What to Prefer
- Short, readable code
- Self-documenting code through good naming
- Direct implementations
- Minimal dependencies
- Concise error handling
- Functional programming patterns where appropriate
- Reusable utilities
- DRY principle (but don't over-abstract)
